<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hyrcanus II</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 30 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hyrcanus II was a Hasmonean high priest and ruler of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/judaea">Judaea</a>, the elder son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-jannaeus">Alexander Jannaeus</a> and Salome Alexandra. Ousted by his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aristobulus-ii">Aristobulus II</a>, he was restored as high priest by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pompey">Pompey</a> in 63 BCE, with the Idumaean <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antipater">Antipater</a> as his chief minister. Captured by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/parthian-empire">Parthians</a> in 40 BCE, he was later executed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herod-the-great">Herod the Great</a> around 30 BCE.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hyrcanus-ii.jpg" alt="Hyrcanus II" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Georges Reverdy · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hyrcanus_II_medal.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
